[
    {
        "content": "<p>I am implementing the <code>#_</code> function from <a href=\"https://plfa.github.io/DeBruijn/#abbreviating-de-bruijn-indices\">https://plfa.github.io/DeBruijn/#abbreviating-de-bruijn-indices</a>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">#_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">suc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤?</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">size</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"o\">)}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"c1\">--------------------------------</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊢</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lookup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">toWitness</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">count</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">toWitness</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>in Lean, and I'm trying to do a proof by reflection which captures the idea behind the Agda definition. I wrote a tactic that grabs a piece of the goal and uses it as a term, where <code>vsharp</code> is the equivalent of <code>#_</code>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Qq</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grab_ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TacticM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getMainGoal</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal_type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getType</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">~</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">~</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HasTyp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferTypeQ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal_type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"nomatch\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">liftMetaTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mvarid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">new_mvarid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mvarid</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">define</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">``Ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">new_mvarid'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">new_mvarid</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intro1P</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">new_mvarid'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">check</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vsharp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- vsharp (n : Nat) (Γ : Ctx) (inΓ : tTrue (leq? n.succ (size Γ))) : HasTyp Γ (lookup (toWitness inΓ))</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ctx</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">HasTyp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(((</span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">conj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Typ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Typ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Typ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nat</span><span class=\"o\">)))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">conj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Typ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">conj</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Typ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Typ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">run_tac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grab_ctx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c\">/-</span><span class=\"cm\"> added the hypothesis</span>\n<span class=\"cm\">  ctx : Ctx := ((Γ.conj (Typ.nat.fn (Typ.nat.fn Typ.nat))).conj Typ.nat).conj Typ.nat -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">vsharp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">unit</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So <code>grab_ctx</code> matches on the goal and adds a hypothesis to the local context, which can be used to prove that the DeBruijn index 0 is within bounds. The <code>Unit.unit</code> term will fail to typecheck otherwise.</p>\n<p>I was wondering, would there be a way to parametrize <code>grab_ctx</code> so that </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">~</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">~</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HasTyp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferTypeQ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal_type</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>is generalized? in other words, turn that <code>let</code> into something like:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grab_ctx_generalized</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lvl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">qsort</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">qterm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inferType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">goal_type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">lvl</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">qsort</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">qterm</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>so that we could have a tactic like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">grab_ctx_generalized</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">~</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">~</span><span class=\"n\">q</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">HasType</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">$</span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>adding the hypothesis corresponding to <code>ctx</code> to the current context? The idea behind the tactic would be similar to the behaviour of</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">conv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">some</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">directions</span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">change</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n<span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">?</span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>where we replace the conv directions with a match</p>",
        "id": 576444951,
